   314→    title: YAML Conventions
   315→    type: feature
   316→    status:
   317→      maturity: draft
   318→      implementation: not_started
   319→    priority: high
   320→    tags:
   321→      - mvp
   322→      - schema
   323→    description: |
   324→      YAML has pitfalls (Norway problem, type coercion).
   325→      These conventions ensure safe, predictable parsing.
   326→    requirements:
   327→      - _ulid: 01KEZCJPJ3Z9T0AWQGEJ3GW2WZ
   328→        slugs:
   329→          - yaml-version
   330→        title: YAML 1.2 Required
   331→        type: requirement
   332→        status:
   333→          maturity: draft
   334→          implementation: not_started
   335→        description: |
   336→          Parsers MUST use YAML 1.2 (not 1.1).
   337→          YAML 1.1 has dangerous implicit typing:
   338→          - "NO" -> false
   339→          - "on" -> true
   340→          - "3.14" might become float
   341→
   342→          YAML 1.2 is stricter and safer.
   343→        implements:
   344→          - "@yaml-conventions"
   345→      - _ulid: 01KEZCJPJ3MFX4H51TN64GEB6T
   346→        slugs:
   347→          - yaml-quoting
   348→        title: Quote Ambiguous Strings
   349→        type: requirement
   350→        status:
   351→          maturity: draft
   352→          implementation: not_started
   353→        description: |
   354→          Strings that might be misinterpreted MUST be quoted:
   355→          - "NO", "YES", "true", "false", "on", "off"
   356→          - Numbers that should be strings: "3.14", "1.0"
   357→          - Special values: "null", "~"
   358→
   359→          The linter should catch unquoted ambiguous values.
   360→        implements:
   361→          - "@yaml-conventions"
   362→      - _ulid: 01KEZCJPJ3M7T6ZNEMTVYBWP96
   363→        slugs:
   364→          - yaml-multiline
   365→        title: Multiline with Literal Blocks
   366→        type: requirement
   367→        status:
   368→          maturity: draft
   369→          implementation: not_started
   370→        description: |
   371→          Multiline strings SHOULD use literal block style (|):
   372→
   373→          description: |
   374→            This is a multiline description.
   375→            It preserves newlines.
   376→
   377→          This is cleaner than quoted strings with \n.
